luci-app-mesh11sd (1.0.0beta)
  * Add - first version, for mesh11sd 8: Status (ubus status and stations, refreshed every 10 seconds, Reload settings), Settings (the setup section in four tabs, keys as password fields, when each option takes effect), Log (mesh11sd read_log, Refresh and Follow) [bluewavenet]
  * Add - rpcd ACL: read ubus mesh11sd status, stations and version, uci mesh11sd and the command /usr/sbin/mesh11sd read_log; write ubus mesh11sd config_reload and auto_config_test, ubus system reboot (Reboot node), and uci mesh11sd [bluewavenet]
  * Add - openwrt/luci layout (luci.mk), tools/feed-sync.sh, translation template [bluewavenet]
  * Add - Settings, General: Run confidence test (ubus mesh11sd auto_config_test) while the running mesh11sd has auto config 0, with a warning that the address changes and the page stops responding [bluewavenet]
  * Add - Settings: Reboot node (notice at the top and on the General tab) while a saved option read only at start differs from the running daemon's [bluewavenet]
  * Add - a header indicator on every LuCI page, and a notice on the Network pages, while mesh11sd runs a configuration not saved to flash (status unsaved_config), since LuCI's own pages show the saved configuration only [bluewavenet]
  * Change - the indicator reads "Mesh11sd live config"; clicking it opens a modal with the explanation, a link to Services > Mesh11sd and Close, instead of adding a notice each time; the Network page notice is never duplicated [bluewavenet]
  * Change - Settings: Country is a list of the driver's countries (iwinfo countrylist), with Default (DFS-ETSI) first, which leaves it unset; a saved value not in the list is kept [bluewavenet]
  * Fix - Settings: CPE mode has one Prefix delegation entry (pd); a saved prefix_delegation shows as it [bluewavenet]
  * Add - Status: mesh path destinations link to the node's LuCI at its apmond ULA (apmond status node_ula prefix plus the EUI-64 of the mesh MAC) when apmond runs [bluewavenet]
  * Add - rpcd ACL: read apmond status and iwinfo countrylist [bluewavenet]
  * Add - Status > Overview: per-radio boxes (ifacebox, green head while up) with type, channel, country, noise, TX power and each live interface, above the wireless table [bluewavenet]
  * Add - Status > Overview: a Mesh11sd section with the live node, mesh interfaces and wireless interfaces (luci-rpc getWirelessDevices, live iwinfo SSID and mode, granted by luci-base, no ACL entry of our own) [bluewavenet]
  * Change - Status: mesh path destinations link to the node's LuCI at the node_ula from mesh11sd status (the same address mesh11sd connect prints), in a new tab; without a ULA the destination stays plain text. apmond is not used [bluewavenet]
  * Change - rpcd ACL: drop apmond status [bluewavenet]
  * Change - needs mesh11sd 8.0.0_beta1-r77 for path node_ula [bluewavenet]
  * Add - Status > Overview: a signal icon on each interface in the radio boxes, as LuCI's own Wireless section: quality from iwinfo for access points; for a mesh point, the strongest peer from the assoclist [bluewavenet]
  * Add - rpcd ACL: read iwinfo assoclist [bluewavenet]
  * Add - Settings, General: Save live config to flash (commit_all) and Revert saved config (revert_all), each behind a confirm dialog; only the relevant button is shown [bluewavenet]
  * Add - rpcd ACL: exec /usr/libexec/mesh11sd-commit-all and mesh11sd-revert-all, which run the mesh11sd CLI after the dialog has confirmed [bluewavenet]
  * Change - Settings, General: Revert saved config is shown when the flash wireless, network, dhcp or firewall configuration differs from the stock copies mesh11sd made before it first ran, not only when commit_all is 1; Save live config to flash is shown when those files still match [bluewavenet]
  * Add - rpcd ACL: exec /usr/libexec/mesh11sd-saved-state, a read-only helper that compares those files [bluewavenet]
  * Fix - Settings, General: Revert saved config runs mesh11sd restore_all, which keeps mesh11sd's own settings so auto configuration rebuilds the live config after the reboot, instead of revert_all, which restored the stock mesh11sd config and could leave auto_config at 0 [bluewavenet]
  * Change - rpcd ACL: exec /usr/libexec/mesh11sd-restore-all in place of mesh11sd-revert-all; the helper clears commit_all first if it was set [bluewavenet]
  * Change - the saved-state helper also compares the system config, as restore_all restores it [bluewavenet]
  * Fix - Settings: do not write Mesh ID seed, Mesh key seed, or other text and password fields that the user did not edit, and turn off browser autocomplete on them, so a password manager cannot commit the LuCI user name and a saved password as auto_mesh_id and auto_mesh_key [bluewavenet]
  * Fix - Settings: Revert saved config was shown on every auto config node, because mesh11sd commits its own portal configuration; the saved-state helper now compares the flash config with the portal copies, and with the stock copies only when there are no portal copies [bluewavenet]
  * Note - possible future version: commit the fixed-role configuration once (portal_detect 0, 3, 4, 5) so LuCI's own pages show the real state [bluewavenet]

